<title>BRAZIL: Brazil mulls tax on forex deals - newspaper.</title>
<headline>Brazil mulls tax on forex deals - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's internal revenue service is considering a 25 percent Financial Operations Tax (IOF) on foreign exchange transactions, a financial newspaper said.</p>
<p>The measure would exclude foreign exchange deals relating to the export or import of goods and services, but would include dividend payments and the transfer of money to raise capital abroad, Gazeta Mercantil said. Factoring operations would also be subject to the tax.</p>
</text>
